{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SJnv28hphVxZrAdxCNS3bN","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Q3 platform review — the queue backlog\n2\t\n3\tSupport tickets to first-response climbed from 42 minutes in July\n4\tto 121 minutes by the end of September. Two things happened at\n5\tonce: the free tier grew nineteen percent, and the on-call rotation\n6\tlost two engineers to a hiring freeze. The auto-triage classifier\n7\tkept up on volume — it labelled 94% of tickets correctly — but the\n8\tlabel it uses for \"needs a human answer\" is a heuristic on token\n9\tcount, and paying customers writing short precise questions\n10\twere routed into the low-priority queue by accident.\n11\t\n12\tWe tried three fixes. Rotating unassigned tickets to the on-call\n13\tpager fixed the tail but doubled interruption cost. Adding a second\n14\tclassifier changed the failure mode but not the rate. What worked\n15\twas smaller: a per-plan priority floor, so a paid ticket never\n16\tfalls below \"medium\" no matter what the classifier says.\n17\t\n18\tThe floor is now live. Backlog is 63 minutes and falling. The\n19\tlesson is that classifier accuracy at 94% still hid a systematic\n20\tmisroute at the tail, and the tail was where our paying customers\n21\twere. We are keeping the classifier and we are keeping the floor.\n22\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7b42e54e-48f5-4c3c-bb27-0a0eafcea1bd","uuid":"e845b6cb-5adb-4111-82cd-ce3c65f9d480","timestamp":"2026-09-10T11:26:50.752Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/cc-pd-skill/article.md","content":"# Q3 platform review — the queue backlog\n\nSupport tickets to first-response climbed from 42 minutes in July\nto 121 minutes by the end of September. Two things happened at\nonce: the free tier grew nineteen percent, and the on-call rotation\nlost two engineers to a hiring freeze. The auto-triage classifier\nkept up on volume — it labelled 94% of tickets correctly — but the\nlabel it uses for \"needs a human answer\" is a heuristic on token\ncount, and paying customers writing short precise questions\nwere routed into the low-priority queue by accident.\n\nWe tried three fixes. Rotating unassigned tickets to the on-call\npager fixed the tail but doubled interruption cost. Adding a second\nclassifier changed the failure mode but not the rate. What worked\nwas smaller: a per-plan priority floor, so a paid ticket never\nfalls below \"medium\" no matter what the classifier says.\n\nThe floor is now live. Backlog is 63 minutes and falling. The\nlesson is that classifier accuracy at 94% still hid a systematic\nmisroute at the tail, and the tail was where our paying customers\nwere. We are keeping the classifier and we are keeping the floor.\n","numLines":22,"startLine":1,"totalLines":22}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_011CeugGjq2edziJsypsdTGN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017SKCVxG2AZafsBjAdEmwFA","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/cc-pd-skill/summary.md","content":"## What\nSupport first-response time nearly tripled in Q3 (42 to 121 minutes) after free-tier growth and a hiring freeze coincided with a subtle auto-triage misroute that dropped short paid-customer tickets into the low-priority queue.\n\n## Why it matters\nA 94% classifier accuracy masked a systematic tail failure that hit paying customers specifically, meaning the metric looked healthy while revenue-critical users waited longest.\n\n## What's new\nA per-plan priority floor is live, guaranteeing that paid tickets never fall below \"medium\" regardless of classifier output; backlog has already dropped to 63 minutes and is still falling.\n\n## What to do\nKeep both the classifier and the floor in place, and treat aggregate accuracy as insufficient on its own — segment tail-latency by plan to catch similar misroutes early.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":605,"cache_read_input_tokens":28148,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":605},"output_tokens":24,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7b42e54e-48f5-4c3c-bb27-0a0eafcea1bd","uuid":"22efaea1-5ff7-4c19-9c29-fe1760a1fceb","request_id":"req_011CeugGjCpVmikLM6sGWHkp"}
